 ### Priority
 
@@ -122,14 +122,24 @@ ### Call Panel (attendant)
 
 Three explicit actions, all deterministic:
 
-| Button | Behavior |
-| ----- | ------------- |
-| **Next (most important)** | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). |
-| **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
-| **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. |
+| Button | Behavior | `App\Enums\CallMode` |
+| ----- | ------------- | ----- |
+| **Next (most important)** | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). | `Any` |
+| **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). | `PriorityOnly` |
+| **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. | `NormalOnly` |
 
 After each call, the ticket leaves the waiting queue and enters the session/display call history.
 
+**Implementation:** `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (`__invoke(Queue $queue, User $calledBy, CallMode $mode = CallMode::Any): Ticket`). It is a domain action with no authorization: the caller (future HTTP/Livewire layer) must verify the attendant may call from the queue.
+
+- **Eligibility:** only `waiting` tickets of the given queue. A **normal** ticket has `priority = 0`; a **priority** ticket has `priority > 0`.
+- **Ordering:** `priority` descending, then `issued_at` ascending, then `id` ascending. The same order applies in every mode (normal-only tickets all share `priority = 0`).
+- **Fairness (`Any` only):** look at the last 3 tickets called in the queue (`called_at` descending, then `id` descending). If there are 3, all are priority tickets, and at least one normal ticket is waiting, only normal tickets are eligible. Calls made in `PriorityOnly` / `NormalOnly` mode count in this history, and a normal call resets the streak. If no normal ticket is waiting, priority tickets keep being called.
+- **Inactive queue:** rejected with `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`, and nothing changes. The queue's `is_active` is read from the database after locking the queue row, not from the passed instance.
+- **No candidate** (empty queue, only normals in `PriorityOnly`, only priority tickets in `NormalOnly`): `App\Exceptions\NoWaitingTicketsException`.
+- **Exactly-once:** the queue row is locked for the whole call. The chosen candidate is then locked and re-checked as still `waiting`; if a concurrent `Ticket::call()` took it first, it is skipped and the next candidate is tried.
+- **Result:** the winner gets `status = called`, `called_at = now()` and `called_by_user_id`, and the updated ticket is returned. Only these three fields change (write-once rule still applies to the rest).
+
